  "note": "Election of the Cookstown Urban District Council, ordinary day 15 January 1931; the four outgoing Unionist members were returned unopposed (Belfast News-Letter, 7 January 1931, p. 9). 'The four out-going members of the urban council, all Unionists, have been returned unopposed. They are Messrs. R. Charles, William M'Clay, William Gough, and William H. Newell.' Returned unopposed."
